WHAT THIS FILE ESTABLISHES
================================================================================

  The post-frontend importCpg verification load, performed by THIS generation
  in clone 13: the independent check that the graph the Joern stages load is
  loadable and non-empty, what its three counts are, and which modules' own
  code it demonstrably contains. A frontend or a record reporting success is
  not evidence that a graph is usable, so every count below is re-derived from
  the artefact itself by the load whose console output is APPENDIX A.

  It is the second of the AAP's four heap-bound JVM invocations (0.5.4) - the
  frontend build, THIS load, the Stage 3 Joern runner and the Stage 5 probe -
  and for each the command, the JDK major version and the heap actually used
  are recorded separately, with the graph's identity re-verified immediately
  before the load.

  HOW THIS FILE IS ORGANISED. PHASES 1 to 3 and APPENDIX A are about the graph
  at the sanctioned path, the one every stage of this run loaded. PART 2, at
  the end of the file, is about a DIFFERENT graph: the per-module witness graph
  of harness/artifacts/logs/cpg-frontend.log PART 2, loaded in its own JVM to
  answer a frontend-capability question. Nothing in PART 2 is a verdict about
  the graph the runners read, and PART 2 states that at its head.

