================================================================================
PHASE 2 - PER-MODULE COVERAGE, BY INJECTIVE EVIDENCE
================================================================================

  The test, stated once and used everywhere: a class present in that module's
  PRIMARY artifact - its main unclassified, non-'original-', non-'-tests' JAR
  - and ABSENT from every other module's artifacts in the same input set. A
  class shared with a same-module sibling still qualifies, which is what makes
  the test satisfiable for a shaded artifact and its pre-shade sibling; a
  class shared with another module does not, because a shared name lets one
  module vouch for another. A shared package prefix is never evidence: every
  Spark module shares org.apache.spark.

  The candidate witnesses were computed by walking all 62 archives of the
  input set and taking, per module, the classes of its primary artifact minus
  the union of every other module's classes. Each surviving candidate was then
  queried in the graph by exact type-declaration full name. 26 of the 31
  modules in the input own such a class; 5 own none.

