  WHAT THIS ESTABLISHES: for every one of the 38 JAR-producing modules, the frontend did
  produce that module's own primary artifact into a loadable graph - the witness resolves in
  the graph in all 38 cases, including the 7 projects that have no archive at all in the
  sanctioned graph's input set and the 5 whose classes are vendored away there. That is a
  statement about THIS graph and about the frontend, and it is exactly why the 12 missing
  verdicts in cpg-module-coverage.json are attributable to the sanctioned graph's input set
  rather than to the build or to the frontend.

  WHAT IT DOES NOT ESTABLISH: coverage of the graph at harness/cpg/spark.cpg. A witness found
  here says nothing about a graph built from a different input set, and the 8 presence-only
  rows would not be admissible as coverage verdicts even for this graph.

====================================================================================================
STEP P5 - the sql/connect/shims collision, resolved by querying this graph
====================================================================================================

In THIS input set the shims primary artifact is present, so the collision AAP 0.5.1 anticipates
is real here: each stub class the shims artifact ships is also shipped by core or sql/core.
Which definition survived extraction is NOT measurable from the frontend's output, so no winner
map is claimed. What IS in the graph is queried and reported.

